## DC 3.4 — Data

### Edit 3.4.1 ⚠️ — Encryption table wording

**Current**

| Data state | Protection |
|---|---|
| In transit (customer ↔ platform, platform ↔ subprocessor) | TLS 1.2 or higher |
| At rest (database, blob storage, backups) | AES-256 (Azure platform-managed) |
| Secrets / keys | Azure Key Vault |

**Proposed**

| Data state | Protection |
|---|---|
| In transit (customer ↔ platform) | TLS 1.2 or higher (HTTPS terminated at the Istio Gateway with per-tenant certificates issued via cert-manager / Let's Encrypt; HTTP is redirected to HTTPS at the route level) |
| In transit (platform ↔ external subprocessor) | TLS 1.2 or higher |
| In transit (within the Azure VNet) | mTLS between pods via Istio service mesh; the NFS share between worker pods and Azure Files runs unencrypted within the customer-isolated VNet (VNet network rules restrict access to API and AKS subnets) |
| At rest (database, blob, NFS, audit log storage) | AES-256, Azure platform-managed encryption with Microsoft-managed keys |
| Application-layer encryption | Selected sensitive fields are additionally encrypted with an application-managed key stored in Azure Key Vault |
| Application secrets | Stored in Azure Key Vault and mounted to workload pods via the Secrets Store CSI Driver and Azure Workload Identity |

**Truth source**: §10 of `system-map-from-code.md`.

